move-hands-children-up for anything but an Untyped:
the tree stays whole and only the moved node's place is lost, which the self-check cannot see.
The replay's prologue moves two made Untypeds, so that mutant shows only the overlap it makes of them.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a move did not keep what was derived from the node it moved

diff --git a/kernel/cap.c b/kernel/cap.c
--- a/kernel/cap.c
+++ b/kernel/cap.c
@@ -119,6 +119,11 @@ void cap_move(struct cap *from, struct cap *to)
      * An only child is its own predecessor and successor, and a root is in no ring.
      */
     *to = *from;
+    if (from->type != CAP_UNTYPED) {
+        attach_beside(from, to);
+        cap_delete(from, false);
+        return;
+    }
     if (from->next != LINK_UP) {
         struct cap *pred = node(from->prev);
         if (pred == from) {
